DESCRIPTION:A participant-led learning community where students\, faculty
 \, and staff meet to explore and critique artificial intelligence technolo
 gy\, and its implications for learners and researchers throughout the Brow
 n community. Learners of all levels and backgrounds are encouraged to shar
 e their experiences\, questions\, and ideas. This week’s topic: Student 
 Panel on AI in the Classroom vs. the Workplace How does AI use differ betw
 een academic and professional settings? Are students being prepared for th
 e ways AI is actually used in the workforce? Join us for a student-led pan
 el exploring how expectations\, pressures\, and norms around AI use change
  between classrooms\, internships\, and full-time jobs. Dr\nCategory: Free
  Food\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/library/event/342316-cri
 tical-ai-learning-community
