UID:8e18da16e6b679770f2cd774f0c4@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Community Service\,Washington\, DC\,United Stat
 es
DESCRIPTION:Join the Office of Equal Opportunity (OEO) in supporting the O
 ffice of Advocacy and Support as we close out Domestic Violence Awareness 
 Month. Enjoy a warm meal and take part in a vigil to honor those impacted 
 by domestic violence. OEO\, along with other campus partners and student o
 rganizations\, will be present to table\, share resources\, and take part 
 in this powerful event and show of support to those impacted by domestic v
 iolence. This space is open to all. Come as you are to share in unity and 
 remembrance. There will be an open mic portion for anyone who is interest
 ed in sharing a poem\, song\, or any other form of expression.\nCategory: 
 Community Service\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/domest
 ic-violence-awareness-month-vigil-6536
LOCATION:Anniversary Park\, F Street between 21st and 22nd NW\, Washington
  DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/domestic-violence-awareness-month-vigil
 -6536
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Guarnaschelli Lecture Series: A Conversation with Helen Shaw — P
 rovidence
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261026T173000
DTSTAMP:20261026T224242Z
UID:71371f28e6226a240a66cacb2629@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Conferences and Colloquia\,Providence\,United S
 tates
DESCRIPTION:2026 Guarnaschelli Lecture Series Criticism and the Theatrical
  Ecology A conversation with Helen Shaw\, Chief Theatre Critic for The New
  York Times Criticism and the Theatrical Ecology brings together The New Y
 ork Times Chief Theatre Critic Helen Shaw and Professor of Theatre Arts an
 d Performance Studies Patricia Ybarra for a wide-ranging conversation abou
 t theatre today. Shaw will discuss the state of contemporary theatre\, fro
 m emerging trends in New York and international theatre to how people are 
 creating work amid shifting financial and political realities. She will re
 flect on the role critics play within the contemporary theatrical ecology
 \, as well as how we might encourage young artists\nCategory: Conferences 
 and Colloquia\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.edu/live/events/3400
 45-guarnaschelli-lecture-series-a-conversation-with
LOCATION:Leeds Theatre\, Leeds Theatre
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.brown.edu/live/events/340045-guarnaschelli-lecture-seri
 es-a-conversation-with
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:brown-arts
END:VEVENT
