SUMMARY:Is There Room for Revolutionary Conservatives in a Liberal Democra
 cy? Lessons from the U.S. and Poland  ﻿ — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261030T150000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261030T163000
DTSTAMP:20261026T224242Z
UID:c4b2ae2f9bd0a04a5f86465d066d@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:In old and new democracies alike\, the right has largely given
  up its traditional instinct to conserve. Instead\, it has adopted the rev
 olutionary tactics once associated with the Left. The United States (Donal
 d Trump case) and Poland (Law & Justice—PiS case) are the two clearest c
 ases in which this “conservative revolution” has gone full circle—se
 izing power\, losing it\, refusing to disappear\, and then returning—all
  while holding on to somewhere between a third and a half of the electorat
 e. The recent Oxford University Press volume Let’s Agree on Poland (eds.
  Maciej Kisilowski and Anna Wojciuk\, 2025) confronts precisely the proble
 ms that follow from this situation\, and forms the basis for this\nCategor
 y: Academic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/is-there-roo
 m-for-revolutionary-conservatives-in-a-liberal-democracy-lessons-from-the-
 us-and-poland
LOCATION:Elliott School of International Affairs\, 1957 E St NW\, Washingt
 on\, DC\, 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/is-there-room-for-revolutionary-conserv
 atives-in-a-liberal-democracy-lessons-from-the-us-and-poland
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
