DESCRIPTION:Join the Women's\, Gender\, and Sexuality Studies (WGSS) Progr
 am for an exciting talk from Visiting Assistant Professor Eva Pensis! Acro
 ss the late twentieth century\, the popular music industry faced a series 
 of scandals in live performance with the widespread use of lip-syncing. Fo
 llowing the advent of recorded sound\, the commercial use of lip-sync in t
 he popular music industry sought to divide the recorded performance from t
 he performer with the aim of controlling both\, most often eliding the vis
 ual presence of African American musicians while profiting from their soni
 c contributions. Framed by the media theorist Moya Bailey's concept of "mi
 sogynoir\," this presentation considers the case of \nCategory: Academic\n
 Original listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/demo-ing-sampling-lip-syn
 cing-commercial-misogynoir-in-post-disco-edm
LOCATION:Rome Hall (Academic Center)\, 801 22nd Street NW
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/demo-ing-sampling-lip-syncing-commercia
 l-misogynoir-in-post-disco-edm
