BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening & Panel: The President and the Dragon — Washingt
 on\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261109T153000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261109T184500
DTSTAMP:20261026T224242Z
UID:291d10bc2ec0b549ebc3b4e635a6@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures & Speakers\,Washington\, DC\,United St
 ates
DESCRIPTION:The Carter Center and GWSPH will host a screening of The Presi
 dent and the Dragon \, a documentary chronicling President Jimmy Carter’
 s decades-long effort to eradicate Guinea worm disease. Since 1986\, annua
 l cases have fallen from an estimated 3.5 million to just 10 worldwide in 
 2025\, bringing the disease closer to becoming only the second human disea
 se eradicated after smallpox. A panel discussion following the screening w
 ill feature: Rochelle Walensky \, former Director of the U.S. Centers for 
 Disease Control and Prevention Christopher Mores \, Interim Senior Associa
 te Dean and Professor of Global Health\, GWSPH Jessica Van Lobel Sels \, A
 ssociate Director\, Guinea Worm Eradication Program\, The\nCategory: Lectu
